Perhaps this would only be applicable to monks and priests or be considered 
meaningless like "shopless" conduct.
This conduct would involve going through the dungeons of doom, and 
associated depths, never picking up gems or gold and relying solely upon 
what you find or steal during your journey.
It could involve never wearing armor above a certain class (leather, never 
metallic or otherwise) or disdaining armor and weapons altogether because 
maintaining a vow of poverty would involve avoiding the attachments of the 
material world.
Anything that an adventurer acquires would be found or created by the 
adventurer like scrolls of enchantment to beef up one's found or "humble" 
items.
What would be the benefit of maintaining such a conduct? Perhaps when one 
visits a priest and they see you are more pious than they are by 
maintaining such a conduct they'd give you the protection one would 
normally pay for in the course of the game to reduce armor class.
Of course this would make the game unnecessarily tougher but I thought I'd 
toss it to the wolves to see what others thought of it.

